"""Atlas content for patches 6.4–6.55, MSQ #835 Currying Flavor to #852 The Game Is Afoot, and the cp-ew-6-55
milestone (after The Coming Dawn, #853). Arc tag za. Data only (docs/atlas/era-modules.md is the contract).

Researched 2026-11-19 from the saved Console Games Wiki wikitext (lanes W25–W28, with W21–W24 read for continuity);
every locator is an exact substring of a quest's Journal, Steps or main dialogue (stage directions inside cutscenes
included). Spoiler rules this module follows:
  - the Endwalker cast reuses the conventional IDs the earlier Endwalker eras should create (char-zero, char-golbez,
    char-azdaja, char-vrtra, char-nidhana, char-jullus, char-erenville, org-loporrits, org-ilsabard-contingent); each
    first presentation here stands on its own as of its step;
  - the satrap is char-vrtra, named "Vrtra" with "Varshahn" (the simulacrum vessel he speaks through) as an alias;
  - the Golbez reveal (#848) follows Marques -> Cid: char-golbez keeps its entry, char-durante is new at #848 with a
    revealed-as edge and "Golbez" as his alias. Durante is named on the #842 page too, but this module leaves him
    unnamed there ("a mage and his comrade"), so the reveal step is the first that shows his name;
  - Igeyorhm is named on #848's page; the text says "an Ascian" instead, so no ALLOW is needed;
  - first names and titles only: no "Leveilleur", "Garlond", "Tsunjika" in text; Wuk Lamat's rival is left unnamed.
"""

def P(frm, until, scope, name, summary, claims, aliases=()):
    return dict(frm=frm, until=until, scope=scope, name=name, aliases=list(aliases), summary=summary, claims=claims)

